From 4a272250f9326f641b958cb71490a16970afb190 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Fick <mfick@codeaurora.org>
Date: Wed, 27 Apr 2011 14:42:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Enable multiple parent project inheritance

Add a new relation object ProjectParent and migrate
the old parent information to this new relation.  Update
the Project object to have plural get/setParents(), and
update all users to be able to handle multiple parents
for a project.  Rename the admin command set-project-parent
to the plural version, also update the command to be able
to clear, set, add and remove project parents.  Allow
multiple parents to be created on project creation. Updated
docs for these commands.

Enhance RefControlTest to be able to make projects inherit
from each other (instead of simulating it by setting the
inheritedRights on ProjectStates).  Add tests to verify
inheritance setup, to test grandparents and the wildProject,
and to test multiple parent inheritance.

Bug: issue 710
Change-Id: Iee4919e40a6aaff63a01b0b680544971c53d23a7
